{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Business Process Model and Notation"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear to talk about BPMN."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Gives information about instruments for data collection. Apply methods for data collection, designing the necessary instruments for information processing, according to the situation set by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  Recognizes basic ideas on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Connectors: Or"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English you can use connectors so that you can do different associations between words and clauses. These connectors are known as conjunctions because they work as links between ideas and give certain emphasis to the sentences they join."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common simple connector are <span class=\"strong\">but</span>, <span class=\"strong\">and</span>, <span class=\"strong\">nor</span>, <span class=\"strong\">yet</span> and <span class=\"strong\">or</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The pattern looks like this:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Main Clause</span> + , +  <span class=\"strong\">Simple Connector</span> + <span class=\"strong\"> Main Clause</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this lesson you learn:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">OR</span>: You can use this coordinating conjunction to suggest that only one option can be performed. It can be used to recommend one thing or another when there are options to choose from."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I can represent a department  <span class=\"strong\">or</span> a complete company by using a diagram.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "These activities can be the major task or sub-processes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are shifts that can be tracked one way or another inside the process."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Business Process Model And Notation (BPMN)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The BPMN stands for <span class=\"italic\">Business Process Model and Notation</span>, and it is a standard model to visualize the processes in a business. Before this model, it did not exist a common language or a common graphical representation in a business process. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The main idea of <span class=\"strong\">BPMN</span> is to use a common language as a model that every business can apply to have a visual representation of its different processes. <br/><br/>  An organization called <span class=\"strong\">BPMI</span> (Business Process Management Initiative) developed this model, which has been preserved by the <span class=\"strong\">Object Management Group</span> since both organizations merged in 2005. <br/><br/>  The diagram is a standard or universal form of representing a process. The main components of a <span class=\"strong\">BPMN</span> are the flow objects, connecting objects, swim lanes and artifacts.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">NOTE:</span> The <span class=\"strong\">Business Process Model and Notation</span> is not part of software engineering but it might help business identification processes. <span class=\"strong\">BPMN</span> is not implemented in software engineering because we use <span class=\"strong\">Use Cases</span> to identify business processes in the area of software engineering."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A BPMN is a model that every business can apply to have a visual representation of its different processes. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fictitious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "fake, invented or a copy of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are going to understand what BPMN is and we are going to create one based on a fictitious example. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "apply "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to employ or use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is a model that every business can apply to have a visual representation of its different processes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pool "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a flowchart it refers to the rectangle that contains lanes to input data "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Basically, the foundations are the swim lanes; they consist of pools and lanes.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "key"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a special item that is important"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Yes, they are key factors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shift "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a change for another person, things, animal or idea "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are shifts that can be tracked one way or another inside the process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "item "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an special article, topic, idea or object"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That is an important item!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about a BPMN."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design and make a fictitious BPMN for a small company. (Remember to use graphical representations)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include information about departments, participants and events of the company in your BPMN . "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your BPMN to your classmates and discuss your ideas. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about BPMN."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create an example of a BPMN for a small company. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I remember the important parts of a BPMN in a company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I Share my BPMN with classmates and complement ideas. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le02ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe8n1le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Margaret: </span> In this lesson, we are going to describe what BPMN is and we are going to create one based on a fictitious example. BPMN stands for Business Process Model Notation, it is a model that every business can apply to have a visual representation of its different processes. The main components of a BPMN are the flow objects, connecting objects, swim lanes and artifacts. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Henry: </span> What are the foundations of these flowcharts? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Margaret: </span>Basically, the foundations are the swim lanes; they consist of pools (rectangles) and lanes. They help us define the participants in the process. For example, imagine the finance department of a company. I draw a pool and three lines. This pool in black represents the whole department and their participants. In each line, I put, in various colors, the activities that every participant does. <br />"}, {"time": "51500", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Henry: </span> And what about other elements like flow objects?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Margaret: </span> Yes, they are key factors in the BPMN. The flow objects are events that normally are represented in circles, then, we have the activities that are symbolized by rectangles with rounded corners. As you remember, I put one activity per area. These activities can be the major task or sub-processes. There is another item, which is the gateways. Diamonds represents them. They are shifts that can be tracked one way or another inside the process. To visually improve your BPMN flowcharting, you can use a variety of connecting objects. You can choose from sequence flows, message flows or associations. <br />"}, {"time": "93500", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Henry: </span> And what is an artifact? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Margaret: </span> That is an important item! The artifacts are data objects, group, and notations. They give extra information and most of the time they are written notations."}]}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe a business process model and notation diagram."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the components of a Business Process Model and Notation, BPMN. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give an example of a business process model and notation. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What models do you know to diagram a business process?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How many programs of graphic representations do you know about?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner: "}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's talk about BPMN"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " An <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">interview</span> with a BPMN expert!"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listenin